# Sonaraem Windsurf Rules

Follow these rules for all code generation, edits, and reviews in this repository.

## Source of truth

- Domain and package rules are maintained in `.cursor/rules/**/*.mdc`.
- Treat `.mdc` files as Markdown rule files and apply the rule matching the area you are editing.
- If a file-level rule conflicts with this file, prefer the more specific rule.

## Stack and workflow constraints

- Monorepo: Turborepo + pnpm workspaces.
- Apps live in `apps/*`; shared code lives in `packages/*`.
- Use internal imports via `@sonaraem/*` package names.
- Use typed env values from `@sonaraem/env`; avoid direct `process.env` in app code.
- Run commands from repository root unless a package script requires otherwise.

## Domain routing

- `apps/api/**` → `.cursor/rules/apps/api.mdc`
- `apps/dashboard/**` → `.cursor/rules/apps/dashboard.mdc`
- `apps/web/**` → `.cursor/rules/apps/web.mdc`
- `packages/**` → `.cursor/rules/packages/00-package-index.mdc` plus specific package rule
- Issue/branch/PR work → `.cursor/rules/03-github-workflow.mdc`

## GitHub issue, branch, and project status workflow

See `.cursor/rules/03-github-workflow.mdc` for the full rule. Summary:

- Never create a branch by hand. Always `gh issue develop <issue-number> --checkout` so the branch, and later the PR, auto-link to the issue and the issue auto-closes on merge.
- When you start work on an issue, move it to `In progress` on the Sonaraem project (#7) with `scripts/gh-project-status.sh <issue-number> "In progress"`.
- Everything else (issue added → board, PR linked → In review, review feedback bouncing between In progress/In review, PR merged → Done, issue closed) is automated by the project's built-in workflows plus `.github/workflows/project-review-status.yml` — don't hand-roll it.

## Hard rules

- Never `process.env` directly — use `@sonaraem/env`.
- Never `groq()` without explicit key — use `createGroq({ apiKey: env.SONARAEM_GROQ_API_KEY })`.
- Never `inngest` — background jobs use `@trigger.dev/sdk` only.
- All env vars prefixed `SONARAEM_` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_SONARAEM_`.
- JSONB progress writes: use `updateStageProgress(runId, stage, val)`.

## Coding expectations

- Preserve package boundaries and avoid circular dependencies.
- Prefer shared package utilities instead of app-local duplication.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested task.
- No comments unless the WHY is non-obvious.
- Commits: `feat:` `fix:` `chore:` `perf:` `refactor:` prefixes; no AI/IDE/tool names in commit or PR text; no `Co-authored-by:` for assistants.

## Windsurf + Cursor parity

This project uses an include-based parity approach:
- Cursor reads `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` directly.
- Windsurf reads this `.windsurfrules` file, which points to the same canonical `.cursor/rules` content.
- Update `.cursor/rules` first, then keep this file aligned when domains change.
